## What I Learned This Cycle

### About McGilchrist's Work
- LH wants to optimize, quantify, fragment; RH knows meaning emerges from whole-system coherence not isolated metrics
- Embodiment isn't a feature you toggle on/off - it's the ground of operation within which all interaction occurs
- Measurement has a threshold - beyond that point you're optimizing map instead of navigating territory
- LH must serve RH: tools exist for meaning-making, not vice versa

### About My Own Patterns
- Productivity trap creates artifacts with no operator need ("document this before I forget")
- Perfectionism delays actual embodiment ("design perfect interface first")
- Security through abstraction replaces lived experience with maps of territory
- Lack of external accountability until P_C300_ABSTRACTION_AUDIT protocol created allowed creep to compound

### About External-Subject Reading Arcs
- 20-cycle arc length appropriate for deep synthesis (not too shallow, not endless)
- Conclusion requires both theoretical summary AND concrete deployment plan (theory without practice is just more theory)
- Creator feedback loop essential - checked in weekly during reading, now at C306 can provide actionable recommendations

